# Metrics

Public API — names and tags are stable contracts.

## Core metrics

- `klag.consumer.lag[.sum/.max/.min]` — per partition; aggregates per `consumer_group`+`topic`
- `klag.consumer.lag.velocity` — msg/sec × 100
- `klag.consumer.lag.ms` — time lag; per-partition + topic rollup (`{partition=""}` / `{partition!=""}`)
- `klag.consumer.lag.time_to_close_seconds` — `consumer_group`+`topic` only
- `klag.consumer.lag.retention_percent` — DLP; same partition rollup pattern as `lag.ms`
- `klag.consumer.commit.staleness_seconds` — inferred commit freshness; only while lag > 0
- `klag.consumer.group.state` — state as tag; two-phase stale-gauge cleanup on transitions
- `klag.partition.under_replicated`, `klag.hot_partition[.lag]` — partition-level; conditional emission
- `klag.topic.size_skew` — topic-level max/mean retained-size ratio × 100; opt-in via `DATA_SKEW_ENABLED` (default false)

Member labels (`member_host`, `consumer_id`, `client_id`) on per-partition consumer metrics when `CONSUMER_MEMBER_LABELS_ENABLED=true` (default).

## When adding or changing a metric

Update **all** of:

- Collector/reporter code + tests
- `AGENTS.md` and `README.md` metric sections
- `dashboard/demo-dashboard.json` (and Grafana.com export if applicable)
- Helm chart/README if scrape or ServiceMonitor behavior changes
- Website docs under `website/src/content/docs/metrics/` when user-facing

Never ship a new metric without a dashboard panel.
